  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "see",
      "title": "See it",
      "text": "The kniroo moves like a knight but takes like a rook. It jumps in an L shape to an empty square, and it captures along a rank or a file, as far as it likes. It can't take on its knight squares, and it can't move to an empty square on its lines. Its name joins knight and rook. In New Zealand chess the knights play this way. The dots mark where it can move, and the rings mark where it could take an enemy piece.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "kniroo" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3I4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4"
    },
    {
      "kind": "try",
      "title": "Try it",
      "text": "Jump to e6 like a knight, then take the black knight on a6 along the rank.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "kniroo" }, "fen": "7k/8/n7/8/3I4/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4",
      "targets": ["e6", "a6"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "read",
      "title": "Strategy",
      "pages": [
        {
          "text": "The kniroo attacks along whole ranks and files, like a rook, but it moves only a knight's jump at a time, so it is slow to get where it is needed. Here it can take the rook on d7 up the file, or jump to e6. It could never move to an empty square like d5.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "kniroo" }, "fen": "4k3/3r4/8/8/3I4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d7"], ["d4", "e6"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "It gives check only along a rank or a file, so look for a jump that lands on the king's line. Here it jumps to h5 and checks the king on h8 up the file, which also covers h7. Your king covers g8 and g7, so it is checkmate.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "kniroo" }, "fen": "7k/5K2/8/8/8/6I1/8/8 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["g3", "h5"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "It can't take along a diagonal, so a bishop can attack it and not be taken back. Here the black bishop on g7 attacks it. The kniroo jumps away, here to b3.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "kniroo" }, "fen": "4k3/6b1/8/8/3I4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "b3"]]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "puzzles",
